    <body xml:id="m-72a2d256-d8ce-43db-a004-79bb9a13a472">
      <mdiv xml:id="m-5c0a44ba-4c75-4c07-b5f5-aa05e4e7fae2" type="solesmes">
        <score xml:id="m-2fef85de-40af-40ed-8faa-6da1262556ed">
          <scoreDef xml:id="m-9f571395-becd-483d-ac49-4bcac6d24662">
            <staffGrp xml:id="m-ebecad21-8e62-461c-900f-3777651411bd">
              <staffDef xml:id="m-3b06f89b-a0b3-455e-be36-30e754ae34a8" n="1" notationtype="neume" lines="4" />
              <staffDef xml:id="m-6c9d1a7f-7b3e-4636-95f7-97638f365a20" n="2" notationtype="neume" lines="4" />
            </staffGrp>
          </scoreDef>
          <section xml:id="m-8a6b5b71-e57d-4c37-922a-4cad786d0149">
            <pb xml:id="m-b5f48e35-6a60-410b-ae7c-b3a08b03f5f0" n="225" facs="#m-104c52f5-d79e-4e67-ae85-d08a734eaac3" />
            <staff xml:id="m-0560d045-8dbe-4202-a2a0-3f05a95894e6" n="1">
              <layer xml:id="m-dcf50d88-f757-47c1-8962-462d5e02f0d8" n="1">
                <sb xml:id="m-d2f96a93-80f8-45cc-bd1c-0b58943a0729" n="1" facs="#m-b0a40505-78ff-42d4-b672-71576663c614" />
                <sb xml:id="m-64d66069-7cdb-4904-8812-9d086122ea1a" n="2" facs="#m-97f91e51-cb65-4c8b-bfb8-603e3c314574" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <staff xml:id="m-d8a31d44-89d8-42eb-a9e8-05e3741ed468" n="2">
              <layer xml:id="m-8b6c412a-7a78-4c4d-8bbc-7f70fd148307" n="1">
                <sb xml:id="m-02d76cd9-ade1-450f-9ad8-a595a851a775" n="3" facs="#m-818e08ea-193c-481c-9bc3-edf5b2e2b2ef" />
                <sb xml:id="m-65ec2846-4be3-4f79-88a6-d8fb5b775367" n="4" facs="#m-45d65d78-c34a-41b3-b06b-6f4bc7c1d768" />
                <sb xml:id="m-a4e9de7f-cd64-4037-880e-3f98433044de" n="5" facs="#m-6ca1e089-9d66-4029-bdce-b04fad51af37" />
                <sb xml:id="m-7e5e5c37-d340-431e-93c4-c0d7a676f599" n="6" facs="#m-5212af7b-13cd-434d-9854-00e9108345ff" />
                <sb xml:id="m-6ecc6b21-58f1-49a4-a50a-ee7a4cca9056" n="7" facs="#m-220217bc-32b5-4f79-8d4f-565d1ab6ce5f" />
                <sb xml:id="m-70461841-e625-4c55-8e38-d27419f37050" n="8" facs="#m-adbd7422-a68b-4767-b714-2393a87335e0" />
                <sb xml:id="m-7eba5219-de7d-43d6-8d66-2c2c20c222de" n="9" facs="#m-49bc62e4-24a1-476a-8c15-10eaae50ebbd" />
                <sb xml:id="m-7aee8019-0af3-486c-8996-e06299b34f4c" n="10" facs="#m-4fe2d1f9-d9de-4c2e-b232-8cfd9e55812e" />
                <sb xml:id="m-21a18f98-e9dd-41c8-8389-aa6d8e81f81f" n="11" facs="#m-40e36762-9b96-40e4-bb02-c17fb5f99389" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-71979323-669c-4b37-97aa-4ab0a7477320">
              <lg xml:id="m-63c8b672-0438-4283-b1e2-6f9531ebd917">
                <l xml:id="m-cb07ac0f-7a56-4cc4-b90c-e90d72310dff" facs="#m-c4919f78-c853-4671-af1a-8ca2a09d95d5" label="ambiguous">113</l><l xml:id="m-bdd92909-593d-45c3-b74c-a3bf6f955054" facs="#m-f28f4fd1-0af1-4338-ae8f-7be3a2ba22a5" label="text-like">The Tones of the Psalms.</l><l xml:id="m-05768562-3d3d-4a18-96ac-f2b44766cedb" facs="#m-99ec495c-0559-49c8-989d-17c177266bcd" label="text-like">Patri, the formula of intonation being reveated by the Cantor at the first verse</l><l xml:id="m-d54e8454-2b01-4471-b977-3737b264f81d" facs="#m-aa17bf28-74d1-4575-b894-b5ea04a6f9b7" label="text-like">or each Psalm or each division. However, the intonation is not repeated ir</l><l xml:id="m-966b8265-0a6a-4c80-a589-5f7c0f6d25bd" facs="#m-6cfe9159-7e86-4652-b0e1-52a19d6260e8" label="lyrics-like">these Psalms are said under a single Glória Pátri. The formula of intonation</l><l xml:id="m-19e71339-150e-4e9f-a9bb-5073b332fd93" facs="#m-0e03adda-0d36-40a0-ac1f-6a1e6ac5c870" label="text-like">is repeated at every verse of the Canticles Benedictus. Magnificat. and Nunc</l><l xml:id="m-1c198c14-b6f6-4e8a-9632-b8250694f45e" facs="#m-c0cdabd5-e112-4938-8d54-a7a867f0c962" label="text-like">dimittis. even in the Office for the Dead.</l><l xml:id="m-d22aed31-0580-4382-b568-c93a08cdc755" facs="#m-53161383-779d-4a82-b87a-11c4793e70ec" label="text-like">For the Canticles Benedictus, and Magnificat. a more ornate modulation was</l><l xml:id="m-76ecff20-e486-498e-ae0b-c4dce9fbc2ee" facs="#m-4dec0ad8-4f64-4686-8fb7-8a274a87f09a" label="lyrics-like">formerly used at the intonation and ãt the mediant in each tone. These</l><l xml:id="m-e05ce14b-88d6-4a02-8820-865de3575b77" facs="#m-3d83ae45-a2eb-4dbf-99be-b2906157bf84" label="text-like">formulas may still be employed at least for the principal feasts. (ist and</l><l xml:id="m-8ba6256a-35df-43c4-9d6d-7d47fc3c9400" facs="#m-70c7873a-dcc6-4737-bb06-2b48cb6e372d" label="text-like">and class).</l><l xml:id="m-32249572-9152-4a60-acf1-417721ec6673" facs="#m-8ea7a1b6-dfea-49cb-b5aa-d50fa38beb54" label="ambiguous">First Tone.</l><l xml:id="m-8985bebc-1c1a-47fc-a85e-8d952ca9ca11" facs="#m-6edab60d-6de2-400f-bf7d-145448e2d51a" label="ambiguous">Terminations.</l><l xml:id="m-d9f88629-ac27-4920-abbd-5807aca15d69" facs="#m-19250ab8-e9fe-452f-b2dd-85abdc5016b7" label="ambiguous">I</l><l xml:id="m-f8208bdc-3e0d-47d5-b50b-f667ee8d5ce4" facs="#m-52f36010-9b7e-4a7f-ba61-69b823cad18d" label="ambiguous">1</l><l xml:id="m-ed3bb8bb-3b34-4cfa-b22e-4969e4f907a1" facs="#m-dba0daf0-e6dd-475d-a0e4-e51090b4fdaf" label="text-like">Mediant of s accent¬</l><l xml:id="m-8e2ddcbd-1cdd-4b2b-b32d-91945b953700" facs="#m-28afcbc6-acba-494a-823f-c6c56cbc5c17" label="text-like">Terminations of I accent</l><l xml:id="m-7a8154a5-170b-4100-bb60-7987abaef41a" facs="#m-f11fc365-f552-46cd-b2f2-2d0410743537" label="ambiguous">D</l><l xml:id="m-25b14e8e-faa8-4f21-a1a0-7fc15c53116e" facs="#m-89752c80-fd7b-49b1-940b-5957c770cbf9" label="ambiguous">vith = preparatory syllables.</l><l xml:id="m-9d0703a0-911f-473d-860e-b7514d7a9310" facs="#m-92334a57-3c77-4be2-8cae-adb104e994cb" label="text-like">Un the termination Da, the</l><l xml:id="m-f68b5090-fc40-4435-bf4a-cd3fb23c1648" facs="#m-778484a6-c4a9-454f-91a8-c77e7464f94a" label="text-like">additional note of the dac¬</l><l xml:id="m-ff8e271f-d0e9-47d7-9fc1-02817e2cfe60" facs="#m-8ea9a36c-104c-495a-87f2-ddd732ee9bd0" label="text-like">tylic cadence is anticipated</l><l xml:id="m-c3de9959-f856-4283-a465-cd3a5698a83e" facs="#m-f76c100a-fd70-48a5-a892-180ac1328cac" label="text-like">vith the accented syllable</l><l xml:id="m-c4bff242-6982-440e-9733-a60563891988" facs="#m-2e0fd283-a5f8-493c-84e0-6126a2e03f61" label="text-like">and precedes the clivis)</l><l xml:id="m-cbddc614-bb86-4228-bc05-1670fe5d05b8" facs="#m-51a66676-0932-4c4e-a4d3-b8254fbc1b47" label="text-like">Int. Tenor and Flex</l><l xml:id="m-9bc44405-a82c-4d6f-9389-c213bc4b4ae1" facs="#m-b2d54cba-5eda-489c-8156-d46e0722d60c" label="ambiguous">Mediant</l><l xml:id="m-5ad828cb-4c85-4428-8ef8-892c3ba40607" facs="#m-2ee8d954-5532-42d3-a850-cdb5fe4fc652" label="ambiguous">Tenor</l><l xml:id="m-9bfb68b6-fb79-4ac0-aa0e-170e69db8f46" facs="#m-383d989f-e732-44a7-8029-8b34da40e39b" label="ambiguous">8</l><l xml:id="m-aa2cf3c1-5fdb-4a0c-ba59-20554da3382f" facs="#m-d8181cff-d3ec-4268-93b9-6ce14eea8945" label="ambiguous">g</l><l xml:id="m-829c1c17-a3e4-43fc-a8aa-50934fac658b" facs="#m-1a212d39-b10b-44b4-8417-6f89a4f25998" label="ambiguous">g</l><l xml:id="m-463d11d4-91bd-4f1c-9dc6-4f0072725587" facs="#m-29148e20-eed2-4e6c-b9dc-c6169800bbf1" label="ambiguous">a</l><l xml:id="m-76c44826-265b-4a86-8843-4c9618901eff" facs="#m-3794f4ff-cb20-4176-a336-ad843a2f52f0" label="ambiguous">a</l><l xml:id="m-7f4ab92d-e28e-401a-b115-0ad19545c791" facs="#m-7e4d8dad-3d5f-4a92-bf08-893ba2e493ad" label="ambiguous">a</l><l xml:id="m-09182884-c5f3-492d-92e2-0cef7ad80a66" facs="#m-54aaacb3-4540-47ee-b86a-895bf5cceb63" label="text-like">"The flex is made by lowering the voice a scond or a third, according to the</l><l xml:id="m-acdf3978-f380-41af-82f4-8a53cbc5af02" facs="#m-bd71eacb-4a93-4cae-ba93-fca760f589a8" label="text-like">tone, on the last syllable before the sign t or even on the second last syllable, if this</l><l xml:id="m-bbbf18e5-03b4-4404-8053-70499e57736c" facs="#m-ff7b07ac-8dd3-45bf-b475-c7638e89ab6d" label="text-like">"lable be not accented. However, a different interpretation is allowed. The</l><l xml:id="m-31c7cf36-a626-486e-a40e-0d6c65bcc36c" facs="#m-afae6446-cf31-4b0c-940e-904658f66ec6" label="text-like">ladexlon of the voice may be replaced by a simple prolongation of the dominant</l><l xml:id="m-43283d5b-a7cb-4862-94d8-e46601cd1164" facs="#m-614a1022-68ec-4f51-9eea-643809cb22b8" label="lyrics-like">temor) and a slight paüse. These rules are applied also to monosyllables and</l><l xml:id="m-f33b8506-ffae-4c3d-8d99-8ef1bc22ee7e" facs="#m-0724e0df-dc76-4bc5-9093-b60883d37208" label="lyrics-like">Hebréw words. (S. C of Rites, July Sth and Dec. 12tb 1912).</l><l xml:id="m-90755a13-a4e9-4874-a68a-d61ca21b90f1" facs="#m-c04af5cd-77f5-42a0-9e0e-05500db0a1ea" label="ambiguous">N°go1.—8</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
